<section id="conclusion" class="closing">
<h2>Conclusion:</h2>
<p>Every item borrowed on Hogshare is one less item manufactured, shipped, and thrown away. Every student who lists something they already own is turning an unused asset into value for someone else while earning a financial gain for themselves. We built hogshare because we saw this problem at NMH, and we believed our solution could help campus sustainability and build a positive community here at NMH. We are not done yet, but we are close, so follow along at @nmh.hogshare and get ready to be a part of something that can truly make a difference right here on the NMH campus.</p>
</section>

